IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nz-nouns`
IMPORT `nz-part1-preliminary`

-- Tests for nz-part1-preliminary.l4 (Part 1, ss 5 to 7).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.

§ `Section 5(1) -- secondary legislation`

-- src:75 | secondary legislation means an instrument (whatever it is called) that—
-- src:76 | is made under an Act if the Act (or any other legislation) states that the instrument is secondary legislation; or
-- src:77 | is made under the Royal prerogative in a form and for a purpose set out in Schedule 1A
-- src:78 | Example
-- src:79 | The ABC Act 2018 enables the Governor-General, by Order in Council, either to make exemptions in the Order in Council or to enable the regulator to issue exemption notices. Both the order and notice are made (directly or indirectly) under the ABC Act (see section 21). The ABC Act states that both are secondary legislation. As a result, both the Order in Council and the exemption notice made under that order are secondary legislation under this definition.
-- The ABC Act example: the Order in Council and the exemption notice are both made (directly or indirectly) under the ABC Act,
-- and the ABC Act states that both are secondary legislation. Both are secondary legislation.
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS TRUE

-- Limb (a) needs both facts: made under an Act AND the Act (or other legislation) says it is secondary legislation.
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Limb (b) needs both facts: made under the Royal prerogative AND in a form and for a purpose set out in Schedule 1A.
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- The two limbs are alternatives.
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is secondary legislation` (Instrument OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 5(1) -- legislation and instrument`

-- "legislation means the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation".
#ASSERT `is legislation` `an Act` EQUALS TRUE
-- The two things the definition names: the whole of an Act, a part of an Act. A Bill is not an Act yet, so the closed "means" leaves it out.
#ASSERT `is legislation` `the whole of an Act` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is legislation` `a part of an Act` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is legislation` `a Bill not yet enacted` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is legislation` `secondary legislation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is legislation` `an instrument that is not legislation` EQUALS FALSE

-- "instrument includes secondary legislation and any instrument that is not legislation": an Act is not named, so the text is silent.
#ASSERT `is an instrument` `secondary legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is an instrument` `an instrument that is not legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is an instrument` `an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is an instrument` `the whole of an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is an instrument` `a part of an Act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `is an instrument` `a Bill not yet enacted` EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:65 | minimum legislative information means—
-- src:66 | the Title of the legislation; and
-- src:67 | the empowering provision; and
-- src:68 | the administering agency; and
-- src:69 | any other information required by regulations made under this Act
-- Closed "means": the four things on the list, and nothing off it. The date of making is not on the list.
#ASSERT `is minimum legislative information` `the Title of the legislation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is minimum legislative information` `the empowering provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is minimum legislative information` `the administering agency` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is minimum legislative information` `any other information required by regulations made under this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is minimum legislative information` `the date on which the secondary legislation was made` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is minimum legislative information` `any other information` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- src:47 | administering agency means, in relation to legislation, the department, Office of Parliament, or other organisation that is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation
#ASSERT `is the administering agency` `a department` `when it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is the administering agency` `an Office of Parliament` `when it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is the administering agency` `another organisation` `when it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is the administering agency` `a person who is not an organisation` `when it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is the administering agency` `a department` `when it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- src:54 | empowering legislation, in relation to any secondary legislation or instrument, means—
-- src:55 | the legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument; or
-- src:56 | the Royal prerogative (for anything done under the Royal prerogative)
-- src:57 | empowering provision, in relation to any secondary legislation or instrument, means—
-- src:58 | the provision of the empowering legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument; or
-- src:59 | the Royal prerogative (for anything done under the Royal prerogative)
#ASSERT `is empowering legislation` `the legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is empowering legislation` `the Royal prerogative` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is empowering legislation` `the provision of the empowering legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is empowering legislation` `other law` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is the empowering provision` `the provision of the empowering legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is the empowering provision` `the Royal prerogative` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `is the empowering provision` `the legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `is the empowering provision` `other law` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 5(2) -- the maker`

-- If the Governor-General is empowered to make the legislation or instrument, the maker is the relevant Minister.
#ASSERT `who is the maker of the secondary legislation or instrument` TRUE EQUALS `the relevant Minister`
#ASSERT `who is the maker of the secondary legislation or instrument` FALSE EQUALS `the person empowered to make it`

§ `Section 7 -- Act binds the Crown`

#ASSERT `this Act binds the Crown` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 6 -- Transitional, savings, and related provisions`

-- src:83 | 6 Transitional, savings, and related provisions
-- src:84 | The transitional, savings, and related provisions set out in Schedule 1 have effect according to their terms.
#ASSERT `the transitional, savings and related provisions in Schedule 1 have effect according to their terms` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 5(3) -- the section 13 definitions also apply to this Act`

-- src:82 | See also the definitions of terms for all legislation in section 13, which also apply to this Act.
#ASSERT `the definitions of terms for all legislation in section 13 also apply to this Act` EQUALS TRUE
